Lab 19: Generate Configuration Files with Jinja2 Templates
Objectives

By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

    Understand the fundamentals of the Jinja2 templating engine
    Create dynamic Jinja2 templates for network device configurations
    Pass variables to templates to generate customized configuration files
    Test and validate templates across different network device types
    Troubleshoot common templating issues and errors

Prerequisites

Before starting this lab, students should have:

    Basic understanding of network configuration concepts (VLANs, interfaces, routing)
    Familiarity with YAML syntax and data structures
    Basic Python programming knowledge
    Understanding of Linux command line operations

Install the required Python packages before starting:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3-pip
pip3 install jinja2 pyyaml
python3 -c "import jinja2; print(f'Jinja2 version: {jinja2.__version__}')"

Lab Environment

This lab is performed entirely inside your own isolated practice environment (a personal Linux VM or Al Nafi cloud machine). All configuration files generated are sample/lab data only and are never applied to production network equipment. The goal is to learn safe, repeatable configuration templating practices that you can later use responsibly with tools such as Ansible.

Your lab environment should include:

    A Linux distribution with Python 3.8+
    Jinja2 and PyYAML installed (see Prerequisites)
    Standard text editor (vim, nano, or similar)

